  <ym-title|Stationary output construction \V draft
  correspondence><label|stationary-output-construction--draft-correspondence>

  Pin <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>; parent session
  hairer-codex-existence-20261111. Output
  <verbatim|manuscript/existence/stationary-output-construction.tex>, initial
  SHA256 <verbatim|1304e0153a9d492a7a9d1aa0cb660714d0033d18151171bec5aeedbc44c61cad>.

  Inspected declarations (namespace <verbatim|YM.Stationary> unless otherwise
  stated):

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Lift/Pathways.lean>:
    <verbatim|Recorded>, <verbatim|relay_ext>, <verbatim|volume_wave>,
    <verbatim|notesPath>, <verbatim|total_ink>, <verbatim|ink_beat> \V
    normalized scalar Taylor coefficient, exact counting volume and finite
    Fourier spanning.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Lift/Ward.lean>:
    <verbatim|colors_align>, <verbatim|harvest>, <verbatim|withdrew>, with
    their immediate finite Ward and symmetry inputs. Common torus recording
    with per-volume error tending to zero gives continuous
    Ward/reality/colour data; convex permutation and orientation averages
    preserve the original coefficient error.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Shape/ClassicalMatch.lean>:
    <verbatim|all_ages>, <verbatim|orbit_cost>, <verbatim|Pointwise>,
    <verbatim|low_columns>, <verbatim|box_unit>, <verbatim|orbit_gate>,
    <verbatim|assembly>. Existing soft-curvature/row-price chapters supply
    atom and row pictures. The new unit expands actual cubic removal followed
    by subtracting that cubic family's fourth coefficient before quartic
    removal. Output classical action excludes the loop term.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Films/LeadingRay.lean>:
    <verbatim|tributing>, <verbatim|TributeColor.crop_edict>,
    <verbatim|iris_resonant>, <verbatim|true_tip>, <verbatim|true_tone>,
    <verbatim|rite_axis>, <verbatim|vanish>, <verbatim|tip_fuel>,
    <verbatim|subtract_fee>, <verbatim|alphaPay>. The proof reproduces linear
    Ward/permutation cancellation, colour-simplicity transverse detection,
    signed reflection parity, the last mixed coefficient killed by Ward, and
    odd cubic cancellation. Quadratic action unit is 1/2; selected scalar is
    twice the real normalized coefficient.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Loops/Curvature.lean>:
    <verbatim|point_quiet>, <verbatim|reach_symbol>, <verbatim|live_wave>,
    <verbatim|draft_pipe>, <verbatim|violet>, <verbatim|achieved>,
    <verbatim|color_pipe>. Same common coarse bed/path construction, exact
    classical derivatives through degree four, invariant moment-zero loop and
    scalar response; real-wave conversion constant is 2*(#Loc G 1)^2,
    including arbitrary momenta. Retains common response-picture and
    inherited-order-four inputs, not a closure claim for their producers.
  </itemize-minus>

  The symmetry arguments apply to leading homogeneous terms only after lower
  terms vanish; reflected-edge phases must not be dropped from full symbols.
  The common picture convention is complex multilinear, not Hermitian, and
  counting site volume, not probability-normalized Haar volume. A
  positive-degree lower jet condition suffices in <verbatim|withdrew>, not
  equality of constant values. The quadratic case obtains its first-jet
  condition from gauge simplicity.

  Literature/canonical reuse: the elementary invariant symmetric
  bilinear-form argument is the self-adjoint part of the existing
  <verbatim|trace-free-rank.tex> colour argument. The quantitative multileg
  source proof is now canonical in <verbatim|multileg-curvature-lift.tex>;
  this unit cites it, not an unverified external lattice-cohomology theorem.
  Atom and row analytic price producers are canonical earlier chapters. No
  external theorem is newly assumed here.

  Commands actually run: targeted <verbatim|sed> and <verbatim|rg> on the
  listed source files and existing manuscript sections; SHA256 captured. No
  Lean source edits/build/axiom replay. New prose remains draft pending
  independent review. Remaining common-picture/transition producers
  explicitly retained in the last paragraph.

